+
+## Conventions
+
+### Command prefix aliasing
+
+Slash commands in this repo always use the canonical `geno-` prefix (e.g., `/geno-mine-extract`). The prefix users type at runtime (`/gt-`, `/geno-`, or bare `/`) is configured in `~/.geno/config.yaml` and applied at install time by `geno-tools install`. Never hardcode aliased prefixes like `gt-` in SKILL.md descriptions or GENO.md.
+
+### Adding a new skill
+
+1. Create a directory under `skills/` named after the skill (e.g., `skills/geno-mine-<sub-skillset>-<verb>/`).
+2. Add a `SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter (`name`, `description`, `allowed-tools`, `license`, `metadata`).
+3. Add a row to the Skills table in this file.
+4. Update the umbrella `SKILL.md` (`skills/geno-mine/SKILL.md`) to list the new skill.
+5. Bump the version in `genotools.yaml`, `pyproject.toml`.
+
+### Versioning
+
+The canonical version is in `genotools.yaml`. The same value must appear in `pyproject.toml` (`project.version`). Bump the version whenever skills are added, removed, or behavior changes. Keep all files in sync.
